# Change 9
my-microservices/
├── Microservices/
│   ├── auth/         # Node.js
│   ├── finance/      # Java Spring Boot
│   ├── messenger/    # Go
│   ├── profile/      # Python Flask
│   └── share/        # PHP
├── docker-compose.yml
└── deploy.sh

+ Use this command to rebuild
docker-compose up --build



+ Each service serves the same routes
  GET /            Home page (Microservices/<service>/source_code/.../index.html)
  GET /health      JSON status: runtime, hostname, uptime
  GET /api/hello   Plain-text greeting

+ Home pages (after docker-compose up)
  Auth      http://localhost:8001
  Profile   http://localhost:8002
  Messenger http://localhost:8003
  Finance   http://localhost:8004
  Share     http://localhost:8005

+ Menu links between services
  By default the menu links to the same host on each service's port (8001-8005,
  or 3000/3001/3002/8080/3004 when the services run directly).
  Behind a domain or load balancer, set the public URLs on each service, e.g.:
    environment:
      AUTH_URL: https://auth.example.com
      PROFILE_URL: https://profile.example.com
      MESSENGER_URL: https://messenger.example.com
      FINANCE_URL: https://finance.example.com
      SHARE_URL: https://share.example.com
